ents are going to  get about a month holiday uh and in some  institutes i have learned that it is  even less than that maybe even two or  two weeks of holiday and in some cases  only just a few days of holiday  which is which is really really  unfortunate but i appreciate that  different institutes have different  constraints and they have to live with  that  but no matter  no matter how short a holiday you have  i'm going to share a few tips okay so  these tips are specifically targeted at  the first year students although i think  that the second year students who are  transitioning to third year will also  find it useful these tips mind you are  not going to add any points in your cv  okay these are general practical common  sense tips this is something to  help you sow the seeds of long-term life  benefits like genuine life benefits and  trust me on this when i say  that this is probably the  last  summer vacation the last genuine real  summer vacation that you're going to  have in a really really long time once  you go into your third year fourth year  once you get your job  you may get  some what is referred to as technically  summer vacation but you're still going  to end up you're still going to go  through the grind of it all okay so  enjoy this summer vacation no matter how  short it is uh savor it okay so let's go  to the tips we have to address the  elephant in the room which is that all  through these six months that you've  spent in your first year you have had to  make many sacrifices to forgo many  enjoyments and one of the foremost  enjoyments for this particular  generation i hope is to sacrifice if you  have done sacrifices that is uh on binge  watching shows from various kinds of  streaming services or maybe even on  television maybe some of you have uh  forgone are playing some video games to  a certain extent maybe some of you are  planning to unleash yourself on binge  watching these shows  and i can understand the temptation but  my advice to you is that  you can indulge yourself a little bit  but don't overdo it okay  there are better things to do as i will  discuss over here  so try to spend as much time as possible  away from screen you have spent  unprecedented amount of screen time  maybe starting even from your plus two  all throughout your first year before  the screen so try to spend as much as  time possible during the short summer  vacation away from the screen okay  whether it is the mobile phone screen or  the computer screen or the tv screen  okay invest this is my first tip to you  invest some actual  uh quality time  outside okay away from your screen away  from your computer get up from your  computer go outside meet with your  friends invest some quality time in  actual physical genuine social  interaction i would like to mention a  point here that especially for the  introverted students the pandemic has  been bad for all of us but  for the introverted students  they may have had  taken the pandemic  as a kind of excuse as an official  excuse to isolate them themselves even  more from social interactions because  they naturally don't feel very  comfortable with these kinds of  interactions and the pandemic just gave  them an excuse to isolate themselves  more okay so if that has happened it is  even more pertinent and necessary that  you try to get out of that comfort zone  of isolating yourself go out and meet  people meet some of your friends some of  your batch mates from school and note  that people who have had online classes  from your home this is your last real  chance to meet up with your school  friends okay your near and dear school  friends because now you'd be coming back  to campus or coming to campus rather my  next tip  would be that  maybe plan out a trip  with your family and friends now this is  rather commonplace advice  people go out on trips in uh these kinds  of vacations so what's new  uh is that  instead of relying on your parents to  plan out the trip  take a 