 yourself okay this is  this will bring immense health benefits  to you and referring back to that  earlier video i made in november 2020  one i had pointed out that health will  be one of the major uh things to look  out for for your success in your  academics okay so this will be a very  very good investment in your personal  development and please also note that  this advice regarding physical  activities about playing games uh is not  restricted to boys i urge all the girl  students also to engage in some kind of  physical activity you may even  just ride the bicycle okay or if you  have a group of friends uh go and play  with them  okay  i know in a city environment this may be  easier said than done but i'm sure  you're all intelligent boys and girls  you can figure out a way for this okay  but please take this very very seriously  i would also like to point out here that  uh going back to that advice regarding  reading  or reading non-academic books  uh see this is  like  a habit which you have to build over  time okay like overnight you cannot  start reading books uh so one tip one  starting tip if you're really not  accustomed to reading books is that  don't try to start read reading books  by taking by picking up something very  heavy  okay it's not going to work out it's  going to absolutely backfire you lose  all interest in reading so my personal  tip is that you start reading  by taking up something very very  interesting on something which you find  a great amount of interest maybe pick up  a very easy kind of thriller okay it's  almost reads like a movie  or  some kind of detective story which is  very enjoyable  i personally enjoy this very much  so agatha christie arthur common doyle  their classics you can go with them or  maybe any modern  techno thriller also but start with  something which actually interests you  next tip is regarding writing now this  is a very very serious tip  you see  this particular generation of students  your generation 